ai_flows.user_message_template:
Raw Inputs:
{{raw_inputs}}

Competitor Context:
{{competitor_data}}

Output a JSON object with: 1 primary 'archetype', 1 'core_tension' statement, and 3 'pillars' (each with a title and 1-sentence description).

Current Brand Context: {{brand_core}}
Slider Adjustment: Tone moved to {{slider_value}}/100 (0=Authoritative, 100=Playful).

Generate 3 pairs of 'How we say it' (Do) vs 'How we don't' (Don't) that reflect this exact tone.

Brand Context:
Archetype: {{archetype}}
Pillars: {{pillars}}
Voice Tone: {{tone_value}}

User Request: {{user_prompt}}

Generate 3 distinct options. For each, provide the text, an alignment score (0-100), and a 1-sentence rationale.

code:
// PLAN:
// 1. Setup & Theming: Inject NU brand CSS variables (Pantone 200 Red, Roboto Condensed, Open Sans, stark neutrals). Strictly adhere to the color system.
// 2. State Management: Main `App` component holds global state: currentScreen, brandCore data, voiceGuidelines, oracleResults, isOracleOpen.
// 3. Components:
//    - Header: Persistent branding and navigation context.
//    - DemoControls: Top-right utility to jump between screens for review.
//    - ScreenIngestion: Dropzone UI for raw inputs with hover/drag micro-interactions.
//    - ScreenProcessing: Animated loading state with cycling text and real AI call to Claude Opus.
//    - ScreenBrandCore: Displays synthesized archetype, tension, and pillars in an asymmetric grid.
//    - ScreenVoiceTuner: Semantic slider that triggers Gemini 3.1 Pro to generate new voice guidelines.
//    - OracleModal: Cmd+K overlay that uses OpenAI GPT-5.5 to generate brand-aligned assets, including copy-to-clipboard functionality.
// 4. AI Integrations:
//    - `ingest_and_synthesize`: Claude Opus 4.6. Parses raw text into structured JSON.
//    - `semantic_voice_tuning`: Gemini 3.1 Pro. Takes slider value (0-100) and generates Do/Don't examples.
//    - `brand_oracle_generation`: OpenAI GPT-5.5. Takes prompt + brand context, returns 3 options with scores.
// 5. Motion: Framer Motion for staggered card reveals, progress ring color modulation, and modal slide-down.

const SEED_INPUTS = [
  { id: 'doc_1', type: 'transcript', name: 'Founder_Interview_Q3.pdf', size: '2.4 MB', status: 'uploaded' },
  { id: 'url_1', type: 'competitor_url', name: 'stripe.com/about', size: 'URL', status: 'uploaded' },
  { id: 'doc_2', type: 'vision_doc', name: 'Aura_Vision_2024.md', size: '14 KB', status: 'uploaded' }
];

const SEED_BRAND_CORE = {
  archetype: 'The Rebel Architect',
  core_tension: 'Institutional Trust vs. Radical Transparency',
  pillars: [
    { title: 'Unapologetically Clear', desc: 'We strip away jargon to reveal the truth.' },
    { title: 'Built for Speed', desc: 'Velocity is our primary feature.' },
    { title: 'Systemic Fairness', desc: 'Leveling the playing field for all.' }
  ]
};

const SEED_VOICE = [
  { do: 'Move money in milliseconds.', dont: 'Facilitate rapid financial transfers.' },
  { do: 'No hidden fees. Ever.', dont: 'Please refer to our fee schedule.' },
  { do: 'Build faster with Aura.', dont: 'Leverage our synergistic platform.' }
];

// Utility to safely extract JSON from LLM responses that might include markdown formatting
const extractJSON = (text) => {
  try {
    const match = text.match(/\{[\s\S]*\}|\[[\s\S]*\]/);
    if (match) return JSON.parse(match[0]);
    return JSON.parse(text);
  } catch (e) {
    console.error("Failed to parse JSON from AI response:", text);
    return null;
  }
};

// --- AI Service Helpers ---
const api = {
  synthesizeBrand: async (inputs) => {
    const prompt = `
      You are a top-tier agency Brand Strategist. Analyze these raw inputs: ${JSON.stringify(inputs)}.
      Synthesize this into a highly opinionated, structured brand identity. Be sharp, specific, and provocative. No generic marketing fluff.
      Output ONLY a valid JSON object with this exact structure:
      {
        "archetype": "A 2-3 word punchy archetype title",
        "core_tension": "Concept A vs. Concept B",
        "pillars": [
          { "title": "Pillar 1", "desc": "1 sentence description" },
          { "title": "Pillar 2", "desc": "1 sentence description" },
          { "title": "Pillar 3", "desc": "1 sentence description" }
        ]
      }
    `;
    const res = await fetch('/api/ai/anthropic', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        model: "claude-opus-4-6",
        max_tokens: 1000,
        messages: [{ role: "user", content: prompt }]
      })
    });
    const data = await res.json();
    return extractJSON(data?.content?.[0]?.text || "{}");
  },

  tuneVoice: async (brandCore, toneValue) => {
    const prompt = `
      You are an expert Copywriter. The brand archetype is "${brandCore.archetype}".
      The user adjusted the tone slider to ${toneValue}/100 (0=Authoritative/Serious, 100=Playful/Irreverent).
      Generate 3 pairs of 'How we say it' (Do) vs 'How we don't' (Don't) that reflect this exact tone.
      Output ONLY a valid JSON array of objects:
      [
        { "do": "Short punchy example", "dont": "Stuffy or wrong example" }
      ]
    `;
    const res = await fetch('/api/ai/gemini-compat', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'x-openai-endpoint': 'chat' },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        model: 'gemini-3.1-pro-preview',
        messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],
        temperature: 0.7,
        max_tokens: 800,
      })
    });
    const data = await res.json();
    return extractJSON(data?.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || "[]");
  },

  generateOracleAsset: async (brandCore, toneValue, userPrompt) => {
    const prompt = `
      You are the Living Brand Oracle. Generate copy adhering to this brand:
      Archetype: ${brandCore.archetype}
      Pillars: ${brandCore.pillars.map(p => p.title).join(', ')}
      Tone Level (0-100): ${toneValue}

      User Request: "${userPrompt}"

      Generate 3 distinct options. Output ONLY a valid JSON array:
      [
        { "text": "The generated copy", "alignment_score": 95, "rationale": "1 sentence why it fits" }
      ]
    `;
    const res = await fetch('/api/ai/openai', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'x-openai-endpoint': 'chat' },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        model: 'gpt-5.5',
        messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],
        temperature: 0.7
      })
    });
    const data = await res.json();
    return extractJSON(data?.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || "[]");
  }
};

